# Testing

- Use the **existing** test runner and layout (Vitest, Jest, Playwright, xUnit, pytest, etc.). Do not add a framework unless the user asks.
- Prefer tests next to code (`*.test.ts`) **or** a mirrored `tests/` tree — match the repo.
- Cover behavior that can regress: API status/authz, pure logic, critical UI flows when e2e exists.
- Skip pure copy/CSS-only changes unless the user asks.
- Deterministic tests: no real network/clock/secrets; mock at boundaries the project already mocks.
- Name tests after the behavior (`creates item for owner`), not implementation trivia.
- Run the project’s test script before claiming done when you added or changed tests.
